Z||000005||Tweek||05-02-2001||02:59 AM||||LOL!!   I had read this earlier, then this evening I went to a friens house to help out with his 79 maro. He had run outta gas and needed me to turn key while he poured gad down carbto make it run long enough to pull gas from tank, as pump was not strong enough to do so while not running. Well timimg was a bit advanced, got a spark and we blew up the 1 liter (plastic) bottle of gas full sending flaming gas all over the motor and paint, all over the lawn and most of his leather jacket was on fire, not to metion the burns on the hand that was holding the bottle. Pretty funny in hindsight, no major damge done, except to his hand. Car already needed a paint job. But hey we got it running. Anyone else ever light a smoke off of a flaming car??  lol<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/tweek.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spektyr||05-02-2001||04:54 AM||||I'm not sure which would be worse... letting the alternator on my Fiero burn, or humiliating the car by peeing on it.<P>I mean I'd hate to see it die a fiery death, but it'd almost be better for it to go up in flames and die, than to have to live with the knowledge that it had been pee'd on.  Poor thing would never be able to stand proudly among the other Fieros.<P>A fire extinguisher is on my list of things to buy, mostly to scare my passengers.  I think if the car actually did catch fire I'd be crying hard enough to put it out.<P>I just love the little girl...<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
